+# Agent Note: Logged input preparation in the local Grok distribution
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-09-06-logged-input-preparation.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+The local SuperGrok adapter projects durable images into smaller request versions, but users and the model cannot reconstruct those transformations from the session log. A per-image cap also fails to bound the complete serialized request.
+
+## Decision
+
+The captured LLM call exposes optional `prepareInput`. Preparation reuses AttachmentStore request versions and returns keyed notices, not image bytes. The host appends notices as existing plugin-sourced user/message events before rebuilding the final input. A visible notice is not duplicated; compaction can remove it and a later preparation can restore it. Adapters without the optional method remain unchanged.
+
+The local provider measures the final serialized UTF-8 body against a configurable 40,000,000-byte conservative budget. It rejects overflow before inference authentication and POST, without omission, splitting, provider fallback, or a claim of successful image receipt. The local standard preset gains the existing generic recall tool; the work-state plugin stays Grok-only.
+
+This is an additive local extension to [the unified image pipeline](2026-08-20-unified-image-request-pipeline.md). That note remains active: its durable storage, codec, cache and other-provider policies are not superseded. No archived record is changed. The local distribution is installed as `0.1.2-rc.1.grok.2`; complete isolated profiles and native production inventory pass. Online model acceptance remains separately authorized.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+**Inject text inside the adapter.** This would make model-visible input differ from the replayable log, so the host owns the notices.
+
+**Build another image cache.** AttachmentStore already owns validated request variants and cancellation; a second cache would duplicate that authority.
+
+**Drop or split excess images.** That changes the requested context or request count without authorization. This provider rejects the complete oversized request instead.
+
+## Testing
+
+Fixed tests cover serialized byte boundaries, repeated image occurrences, cancellation, failure before POST, logged notice reconstruction, compaction restoration, both installed profile compositions, old-log rollback reads and unchanged Bridge request counting. Local HTTP requests also check compression-header negotiation. Online acceptance requires a separate current authorization.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Preparing an image does not prove provider receipt. Notices add tokens and must count toward the final body budget. A new host/provider package pair must be installed together; unit tests alone do not prove full profile compatibility.
